Command Code: steer mid-turn sends instead of failing them.

Upstream PR #10861 rejects any `sendTurn` that arrives while a turn is
running with "a turn is already running for this thread". Every other
provider adapter treats that case as a steer, and T3 clients send mid-turn
messages on purpose, so the user's message is dropped and the thread records
a turn-start failure (observed 2026-09-16 on a long-running turn).

Command Code headless mode takes one prompt per `-p` process, so the message
cannot reach the live child. The adapter now queues it on the active run and
runs it as the same turn once that process exits, resuming the same Command
Code session — no new `turn.started`, one `turn.completed` when the queue is
empty. The queue check and the release share a single update so a steer can
never land on a run that will not drain again.

